    "result_text": "Full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, the response (and the persisted owner read back via `GET`) now carries `bulkSignupWarning`: `true` when more than 80 owners were already registered on that owner's business day at the moment of creation, `false` otherwise.\n\nThe work landed where each piece belongs, reusing existing machinery rather than duplicating it:\n\n- **`OwnerRepository.countRegisteredOn(LocalDate)`** \u2014 a new default method that owns the \"how many owners are registered on a given day\" query. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` was refactored to call it instead of its own inline stream, so the daily-limit rule and the bulk warning share one accumulation path (as the test comment expects).\n- **`FlagBulkSignup`** \u2014 a new single-responsibility pipeline step (mirroring `CountNamesakes`) that runs after `ResolveRegistrationDate` and before `SaveOwner`, so it keys off the adjusted date and counts only pre-existing owners. It holds the `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and sets the flag on the entity.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `flagBulkSignup` into the transactional pipeline between `ensureDailyOwnerLimit` and `assignCustomerCode`.\n- **`Owner`** entity + all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`/`h2`/`postgres`/`mysql`) \u2014 a persisted `bulk_signup_warning` column so the creation-time snapshot survives the `GET` reload.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema; MapStruct auto-maps it by name into `OwnerDto`.\n\n`./mvnw test` is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
